      "lastReply": "A VPN is a private tunnel between your device and the internet: your traffic is locked, sent to the VPN company's computer, and only then goes out to the website.\n\nWithout a VPN: your internet provider and the Wi-Fi owner can see which sites you visit, and the sites see your real location.\nWith a VPN: they only see scrambled data going to one place, the VPN. The website sees the VPN's location, not yours.\n\nThink of it as posting a sealed letter inside another envelope addressed to a friend, who then forwards it for you. Handy on public Wi-Fi, or to hide your location. It doesn't make you anonymous though, since the VPN company can still see your traffic, so pick one you trust.\n\n9:54 PM",
